# Python
__pycache__/
*.pyc
.venv/
venv/
.pytest_cache/

# osmnx's own download cache. Handy locally - it makes a rebuild of the map take
# 8 seconds instead of 220 - but it is a cache of someone else's server's
# answers, not our data. The committed files in backend/data/ are what the
# deploy actually reads.
backend/cache/

# Local secrets — never commit the real one, only .env.example
.env

# The reports database is generated at runtime
backend/data/amparo.db

# NOTE: backend/data/graph_cache.graphml and backend/data/pois.json are
# DELIBERATELY NOT ignored. They are the prebuilt map and the prebuilt list of
# places, and a deploy without them downloads both live from a rate-limited
# public server while the judge watches a spinner. Commit them. Together they
# are under 1 MB, and they take startup from 220 seconds to half a second.

# Frontend
node_modules/
frontend/dist/

# The built frontend that FastAPI serves.
#
# COMMITTED ON PURPOSE, like the map cache above, and for a related reason:
# the server that runs this is a Python server. It has no Node, so it cannot
# run `npm run build` itself. Shipping the built files means the deploy is
# exactly what you tested on your own machine, and the whole install is one
# `pip install`.
#
# The cost is that you must remember to rebuild before you push:
#     cd frontend && npm run check
# Miss it and the site is live but showing yesterday's frontend, which is a
# confusing thing to debug at 2am. See DEPLOY.md.

# Editors / OS
.vscode/
.idea/
.DS_Store
